### Vocabulary collisions

- Against `error/warning/info`: ext `Critical` (:186), unprefixed `Required` (:185), `Optional`/`Consider` (:188), `Nit` (:187), `FYI` (:189); the ext review-agent prompt says "Flag any issues as Critical, Required, Optional, or Nit." (:230).
- Against `auto-fix/no-op/ask-user`: ext author actions "Must address before merge", "Author may ignore", "No action needed" (:185-189) and "Ask before deleting" (:239) compete with nm 203549-203551.
- Against `working/needs-decision/blocked/paused/done/failed`: ext "Blocks merge" (:186) and "Presumptive blockers" (:398) are about merge readiness, while firstmate's `blocked:` means a stuck worker who needs firstmate (`bin/fm-brief.sh`:182); ext "Approve" / "Request changes" (:348-349) is a verdict no firstmate state carries and collides with no-mistakes approval gates.
- A worker loading this skill would put these labels into its findings and status output, which is exactly the foreign vocabulary the staged-trial criterion forbids.

